From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Kamil=20Postro=C5=BCny?= <kamil@postrozny.pl>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 04:06:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: iOS: replace a read-only link a file is created over

The prefix's system32, syswow64 and sysarm64 are symbolic links into the
app bundle, which is read-only. An installer that writes its own copy of
a DLL Wine also builds (the VC++ 2015-2022 redistributable's MSI writes
concrt140.dll, msvcp140.dll and vcruntime140.dll into syswow64) opened
the link with FILE_OVERWRITE_IF and got STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED, so its
InstallFiles action failed (FDICopy failed, 1603). On a desktop prefix
these are plain files and the write succeeds. For FILE_SUPERSEDE and
FILE_OVERWRITE_IF, a link whose target cannot be written is removed
first, and the file is created in its place. The app relinks every
bundle DLL at the next session start, so the runtime's DLLs come back
then; files the bundle does not have (mfc140u.dll) stay.

Class: host-app
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-11-uepre-authenticode.md
Offered-upstream: no; iOS-only (the bundle links are Playport's)
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
index 1975cc6..c6b7a28 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -4747,6 +4747,22 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtCreateFile( HANDLE *handle, ACCESS_MASK access, OBJECT_ATTRIBU
     if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS)
     {
         name_hidden = is_hidden_file( unix_name );
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+        /* The prefix's system32, syswow64 and sysarm64 are links into the app
+         * bundle, which cannot be written. A file created over one replaces the
+         * link with a file of its own, as on a desktop prefix, where these are
+         * plain files: an installer writing its own msvcp140.dll or
+         * concrt140.dll (the VC++ redistributable) otherwise fails with access
+         * denied. The app relinks every bundle DLL at the next session start. */
+        if (!created && (disposition == FILE_SUPERSEDE || disposition == FILE_OVERWRITE_IF))
+        {
+            struct stat st;
+            if (!lstat( unix_name, &st ) && S_ISLNK( st.st_mode ) &&
+                faccessat( AT_FDCWD, unix_name, W_OK, 0 ) &&
+                (errno == EACCES || errno == EPERM || errno == EROFS) && !unlink( unix_name ))
+                TRACE( "replaced the read-only link %s\n", debugstr_a(unix_name) );
+        }
+#endif
         status = open_unix_file( handle, unix_name, access, &new_attr, attributes,
                                  sharing, disposition, options, ea_buffer, ea_length );
 #ifdef WINE_IOS
